---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const methodologySchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "headline": "VoltSavings Calculation Methodology, Mathematical Equations & Computational Architecture",
  "description": "Comprehensive documentation of the mathematical formulas, energy density conversion factors, onboard charging losses, and empirical data sources powering the VoltSavings calculator.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "VoltSavings Research Team"
  }
};
---

<Layout 
  title="Calculation Methodology & Mathematical Formulas | VoltSavings™"
  description="Explore the transparent mathematical formulas, energy conversion factors, onboard AC-to-DC charging losses, and maintenance assumptions powering VoltSavings."
  schema={methodologySchema}
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 lg:py-16 w-full flex-grow">
    
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
      { name: 'Methodology' }
    ]} />

    <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm">
      
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="mb-10 border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600">E-E-A-T & MATHEMATICAL TRANSPARENCY</span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-950 tracking-tight mt-2">Calculation Methodology</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-2 font-medium">
          Comprehensive scientific documentation of equations, energy conversion factors, and vehicle benchmarks powering the VoltSavings engine.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-700 font-medium leading-relaxed">
        
        <p>
          At <strong>VoltSavings</strong>, we believe computational financial tools must be fully open and auditable. We do not use proprietary "black-box" estimation algorithms. Below is the complete mathematical model, thermodynamic loss considerations, and environmental emission formulas implemented in our client-side software.
        </p>

        <!-- Equation 1 -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-3xl">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-emerald-600 text-white font-black text-xs flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-950">Commute Volume & Distance Equations</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-4">
            Total monthly distance is computed by multiplying the single-day round-trip commuting distance by the user's active travel days per month:
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-2xl font-mono text-xs text-gray-900 font-bold space-y-1.5 shadow-xs">
            <p>Monthly Distance (km) = Daily Commute (km) × Commute Days Per Month</p>
            <p>Annual Distance (km) = Monthly Distance × 12</p>
            <p>5-Year Distance (km) = Monthly Distance × 60</p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-gray-500 mt-3 font-normal">
            *Default configuration assumes standard 26 active working/commute days per month (6-day work week) or customizable via daily slider.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Equation 2 -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-3xl">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-red-600 text-white font-black text-xs flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-950">Internal Combustion Engine (ICE / Petrol) Model</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-4">
            Liquid fuel volume consumed is derived from distance divided by verified operational fuel economy, combined with recurring monthly mechanical upkeep:
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-2xl font-mono text-xs text-red-950 font-bold space-y-1.5 shadow-xs">
            <p>Fuel Volume Consumed (L) = Monthly Distance (km) ÷ Fuel Economy (km/L)</p>
            <p>Direct Monthly Fuel Cost = Fuel Volume Consumed (L) × Fuel Price Per Liter</p>
            <p>Total Monthly ICE Cost = Direct Monthly Fuel Cost + ICE Monthly Maintenance</p>
            <p>ICE Cost Per Kilometer = Total Monthly ICE Cost ÷ Monthly Distance</p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-3">
            <strong>ICE Maintenance Factors:</strong> Periodic motor oil changes (semi-synthetic or full synthetic every 3,000-5,000 km), oil filters, air filters, spark plugs, drive belts, and friction brake pads.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Equation 3 -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-3xl">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-emerald-600 text-white font-black text-xs flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-950">Electric Vehicle (EV) Energy Consumption Model</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-4">
            Electric vehicle energy is calculated in kilowatt-hours (kWh). One kWh equals one standard unit of domestic electricity billed by residential utility providers:
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-2xl font-mono text-xs text-emerald-950 font-bold space-y-1.5 shadow-xs">
            <p>Delivered Battery Energy (kWh) = Monthly Distance (km) ÷ EV Efficiency (km/kWh)</p>
            <p>Grid Energy Draw (kWh) = Delivered Battery Energy ÷ Charging Efficiency Factor (η ≈ 0.88)</p>
            <p>Direct Monthly Charging Cost = Grid Energy Draw (kWh) × Electricity Tariff Rate</p>
            <p>Total Monthly EV Cost = Direct Monthly Charging Cost + EV Monthly Maintenance</p>
            <p>EV Cost Per Kilometer = Total Monthly EV Cost ÷ Monthly Distance</p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-3">
            <strong>Onboard AC-to-DC Conversion Loss (η):</strong> Level 1 and Level 2 AC home wall chargers typically exhibit an 10% to 15% thermodynamic conversion loss through onboard rectifiers and thermal battery cooling circuits. Our default presets factor this real-world draw into overall consumption.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Equation 4 -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-3xl">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-teal-600 text-white font-black text-xs flex items-center justify-center">4</span>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-950">Net Retained Cash & Compounding Multi-Year ROI</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-4">
            Net savings quantify the exact discretionary cash retained in the commuter's wallet by avoiding fuel station visits and mechanical servicing:
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-2xl font-mono text-xs text-teal-950 font-bold space-y-1.5 shadow-xs">
            <p>Monthly Retained Savings = Max(0, Total Monthly ICE Cost - Total Monthly EV Cost)</p>
            <p>Percentage Saved (%) = Round((Monthly Retained Savings ÷ Total Monthly ICE Cost) × 100)</p>
            <p>Annual Savings (Year 1) = Monthly Retained Savings × 12</p>
            <p>3-Year Cumulative Savings = Monthly Retained Savings × 36</p>
            <p>5-Year Cumulative Savings = Monthly Retained Savings × 60</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Equation 5 -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-3xl">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-cyan-700 text-white font-black text-xs flex items-center justify-center">5</span>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-950">Environmental Tailpipe Emissions Avoided</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-4">
            Based on established environmental chemistry standards (US EPA and Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change guidelines), the combustion of 1 liter of standard automotive gasoline generates approximately 2.31 kilograms of carbon dioxide (CO₂):
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-2xl font-mono text-xs text-cyan-950 font-bold space-y-1.5 shadow-xs">
            <p>Avoided Monthly CO₂ (kg) = Fuel Volume Consumed (Liters) × 2.31 kg CO₂ / Liter</p>
            <p>Avoided Annual CO₂ (Tons) = (Avoided Monthly CO₂ × 12) ÷ 1,000</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Vehicle Efficiency Benchmarks Table -->
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10">Empirical Vehicle Efficiency Benchmarks (2026 Reference)</h2>
        <p>
          To ensure accurate comparisons across diverse vehicle segments, our pre-calibrated presets are anchored against extensive real-world automotive telemetry:
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto bg-white rounded-3xl border-2 border-gray-200 shadow-xs">
          <table class="w-full text-xs text-left border-collapse">
            <thead class="bg-gray-100 text-gray-950 font-black uppercase text-[11px] border-b border-gray-200">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 sm:p-4">Vehicle Category</th>
                <th class="p-3 sm:p-4">ICE Fuel Economy</th>
                <th class="p-3 sm:p-4 text-emerald-700">EV Efficiency Benchmark</th>
                <th class="p-3 sm:p-4">Typical Battery Pack</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200">
              <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-gray-950">Electric Scooter (Intra-city)</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">50 - 65 km/L (70cc)</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 text-emerald-700 font-bold">35 - 50 km/kWh</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">1.5 - 2.5 kWh</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-gray-950">Commuter Motorcycle (125cc-150cc)</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">38 - 48 km/L</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 text-emerald-700 font-bold">25 - 35 km/kWh</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">3.0 - 5.0 kWh</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-gray-950">Subcompact Hatchback (1.0L - 1.2L)</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">15 - 19 km/L</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 text-emerald-700 font-bold">7.0 - 8.5 km/kWh</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">30 - 45 kWh</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-gray-950">Mid-size Sedan (1.5L - 2.0L)</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">12 - 16 km/L</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 text-emerald-700 font-bold">5.5 - 7.2 km/kWh</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">55 - 75 kWh</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-gray-950">Compact SUV / Crossover</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">9 - 13 km/L</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 text-emerald-700 font-bold">4.2 - 5.5 km/kWh</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">65 - 85 kWh</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-gray-950">Commercial Light Delivery Van</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">7 - 10 km/L (Diesel)</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 text-emerald-700 font-bold">3.0 - 4.2 km/kWh</td>
                <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">80 - 120 kWh</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10">Real-World Environmental & Climate Disclosures</h2>
        <p>
          While our model provides exact direct mathematical projections, real-world operational efficiency can vary based on external factors:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs text-gray-700 font-semibold">
          <li><strong>Extreme Ambient Temperature:</strong> Under severe winter temperatures (below 0°C / 32°F) or scorching heat (above 42°C / 108°F), cabin heating and air conditioning loads can reduce electric driving range by 15% to 25%.</li>
          <li><strong>Aerodynamic Highway Drag:</strong> At sustained highway speeds exceeding 110 km/h (68 mph), aerodynamic resistance increases exponentially, slightly favoring liquid fuels on continuous long-distance transit.</li>
          <li><strong>Battery Aging & Capacity Fade:</strong> Modern LFP packs degrade gradually (approximately 1% to 1.5% per year). For a full technical analysis of battery chemistry lifecycles, read our <a href="/blog/ev-battery-life-2026" class="text-emerald-600 font-bold underline">EV Battery Lifespan & Degradation Guide</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <!-- Internal Links to Guides -->
        <div class="mt-8 p-6 bg-emerald-50/70 border border-emerald-200 rounded-3xl">
          <strong class="text-sm font-black text-emerald-950 block mb-2">Related Research & Articles</strong>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-800">
            <li><a href="/blog/ev-savings-2026" class="hover:underline">→ How Much Money Do You Save Switching to an EV? (2026 Cost Study)</a></li>
            <li><a href="/blog/ev-bikes-2026" class="hover:underline">→ Are Electric Motorcycles Worth It for Daily Commuters?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/blog/ev-battery-life-2026" class="hover:underline">→ EV Battery Lifespan, LFP Chemistry & Replacement Cost Guide</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Action Footer -->
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center justify-between">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-black text-gray-950">Test these formulas with your own commute</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-medium">Free interactive simulator with real-time currency conversion.</p>
        </div>
        <a 
          href="/#calculator-app" 
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl text-xs font-bold bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 text-white shadow-md shadow-emerald-600/25 transition-all"
        >
          Open Free Calculator <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
